  "id": "disorganized-schizophrenia",
  "term": "disorganized schizophrenia",
  "definition": "Disorganized schizophrenia is a subtype of schizophrenia marked by disorganized speech and behavior along with flat or inappropriate emotional expression. It may also involve grimacing, mannerisms, and other unusual behaviors, without meeting the pattern described for the catatonic type.",
